<h4 class="dialog-section-title">What Can You Expect During Training?</h4>
<ul class="dialog-list">
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Precise and progressive mastery of fundamental techniques (kihon)</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Traditional formal exercises (kata) and the practical application of their underlying principles (bunkai)</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Partner-based self-defense and traditional sparring exercises (kumite)</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Dedicated strength, stretching, and overall conditioning drills</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Biannual belt examinations providing an opportunity to showcase your newly acquired skills</li>
</ul>
<h4 class="dialog-section-title">Who Is It For?</h4>
<ul class="dialog-list">
	<li><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i> Anyone from age 6 upwards, irrespective of gender or prior martial arts background</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i> Those eager to immerse themselves in the deeper, traditional heritage of karate</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i> Individuals simply looking to enjoy an excellent workout and maintain their physical health</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i> Anyone who wishes to become part of a genuinely cohesive and supportive community</li>
	<li><i class="fas fa-user-check"></i> Competitors who are specifically passionate about mastering formal exercises (kata)</li>
</ul>
